---
// Invariant C, shape #4: the SAME key under its bare name, with no `SUPABASE_` prefix.
//
// The prefix is a convention about which service an environment variable belongs to, not
// part of the key's identity. A module that destructures the value, re-exports it, or
// reads it out of a config object under the short name holds exactly the same credential,
// and a rule that only knew the prefixed spelling would read this page and find nothing.
//
// This spelling is also what decides whether a two-literal concatenation of the PREFIXED
// name is caught: split it after the prefix and the second literal is exactly the name
// below, so the scan matches that fragment — not because the build folded anything back
// together, but because the fragment is itself banned. Split it anywhere else and nothing
// matches; see src/lib/runtime-named-key.ts, which pins that half.
const serviceRoleKey = import.meta.env.SERVICE_ROLE_KEY;
---

<p>{serviceRoleKey ? 'configured' : 'absent'}</p>
